'pv.m.fluxoT':'How the forecast is built',
'pv.m.p1':'<b>Historical output.</b> The model reads the state output series consolidated by Squad 1 from ANM: 2010–2025 (bauxite from 2014). Only observed, validated rows are used; duplicates or negative values stop the run.',
'pv.m.p2':'<b>Energy intensity.</b> For each mineral, the electricity the operations drew in the CCEE in 2025 is divided by their output in the same year (MWh per tonne). Bauxite, with no load identified in the CCEE, uses an external benchmark.',
'pv.m.p3':'<b>Backtest.</b> The last two years of each series are held out and forecast from the earlier years, comparing the historical trend with simply repeating the last value. The error (MAPE) guides the rule for each mineral.',
'pv.m.p4':'<b>Scenarios.</b> Output is projected from 2027 to 2040 with the historical compound growth plus each scenario adjustment, and energy intensity falls with the annual efficiency gain. Energy = output × intensity.',
'pv.m.p5':'<b>Uncertainty.</b> Each value gets a low–high range combining the backtest error with ±10% on the energy intensity.',
'pv.m.eqT':'Equations',
'pv.m.eq':'Output(m, t)      = Output(m, 2025) × (1 + g(m) + scenario adjustment)^(t − 2025)\nIntensity(m, t)   = MWh/t(m) × (1 − efficiency gain)^(t − 2025)\nEnergy(m, t)      = Output(m, t) × Intensity(m, t)\nTotal(t)          = Σ Energy(m, t) over the five minerals\n\nOutput with projects(m, t, s) = Output(m, t) + Σ weight(maturity, s) × project increment(t)',
'pv.m.eqNota':'g(m) is the compound growth rate of the mineral historical series. Tonnes are not added across minerals; only energy is aggregated.',
'pv.m.cenT':'Scenario assumptions',
'pv.m.cenSub':'Adjustment on each mineral historical growth and annual energy-efficiency gain.',
